From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:16:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: apple: allow SuperSpeed Plus on T8132
 ports by default

The T8132 Type-C ports' controllers are DWC_usb31 cores; macOS names
their buses "USB 3.1 Bus" and runs a 10 Gb/s device at 10 Gb/s. Here the
devicetree's maximum-speed = "super-speed" makes dwc3_core_init() force
Gen 1, and t8132_usb_gen2, which lifts that cap per cable session, was
off by default: every USB 3 device ran at 5 Gb/s at most.

Turn t8132_usb_gen2 on by default. A link that does not train at Gen 2
falls back as any SuperSpeed link does, and the parameter still caps
the next cable session at Gen 1 when cleared.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
index e435939a17..4e0feac7cb 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -865,19 +865,19 @@ static bool dwc3_apple_host_only(struct device *dev)
 	       of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t6050-dwc3");
 }
 
-static bool t8132_usb_gen2;
+static bool t8132_usb_gen2 = true;
 module_param(t8132_usb_gen2, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_usb_gen2,
-		 "T8132: let a Type-C port's USB 3.1 controller run SuperSpeed Plus (USB 3.2 Gen 2, 10 Gb/s), as macOS's \"USB 3.1 Bus\" does; applies at the next cable (default off)");
+		 "T8132: let a Type-C port's USB 3.1 controller run SuperSpeed Plus (USB 3.2 Gen 2, 10 Gb/s), as macOS's \"USB 3.1 Bus\" does; applies at the next cable (default on)");
 
 /*
  * The T8132 ports' controllers are DWC_usb31 cores, and macOS names their buses "USB 3.1 Bus".
  * The devicetree caps them at maximum-speed = "super-speed", for which dwc3_core_init() sets
  * LLUCTL.FORCE_GEN1 and the link never tries 10 Gb/s. With t8132_usb_gen2, a cable session
  * starts with the cap lifted, as Aurora's J575c (T6041) runs its ports with no maximum-speed:
- * SuperSpeed Plus, one lane at Gen 2. Whether this ATC PHY trains at Gen 2 is for a device to
- * show; a link that does not falls back as any SuperSpeed link does. Cleared, the next cable
- * session is capped as the devicetree says again.
+ * SuperSpeed Plus, one lane at Gen 2. It is on by default, so that a 10 Gb/s device gets 10 Gb/s
+ * as under macOS; a link that does not train at Gen 2 falls back as any SuperSpeed link does.
+ * Cleared, the next cable session is capped as the devicetree says again.
  */
 static void dwc3_apple_usb_gen2(struct dwc3_apple *appledwc)
 {
-- 
2.43.0

